id: templates/node
title: "templates node"
kind: mental-model-node
record_shape: header
authored_by: unattributed  # dave-human | agent-on-behalf | yawn.bot | unattributed
status: active-mixed
updated: 2026-09-13

purpose: >
  Hold reusable .yawn shapes that people and agents can copy without learning
  the whole ontology.

holds:
  - basic template
  - observation template
  - observation-question-art template
  - orientation shape template
  - feedback template
  - full template
  - decision template
  - relationship template
  - proof template
  - proof receipt template
  - agent handoff template
  - access record template
  - backup record template
  - next-move record template
  - open-question template
  - arena template
  - asynchronous turn template
  - structural routing proposal template
  - structural change receipt template
  - objective holon template
  - mental model template (questions first)
  - orientation_inquiry projection fields over an independent orientation_map
  - seal, answer, and floor templates (the articulation-floor loop)

record_shapes:
  canonical: header
  rule: >
    Every template declares record_shape:. header is canonical for new human-readable
    records. spec-version and coordinate are working-draft contract shapes kept until their
    own migration receipt. fragment is a partial record meant to be embedded, never a file
    on its own. json-contract is machine-validated and not human-readable-first; see
    JUDGMENTS.md §2B on audience-primacy before adding another.
  files:
    access-record.yawn: header
    agent-handoff.yawn: header
    backup-record.yawn: header
    basic.yawn: header
    decision.yawn: header
    feedback.yawn: header
    full.yawn: header
    mental-model.yawn: header
    next-move-record.yawn: header
    observation-question-art.yawn: header
    open-question.yawn: header
    orientation-shape.yawn: header
    proof.yawn: header
    proof-receipt.yawn: header
    relationship.yawn: header
    seal.yawn: header
    answer.yawn: header
    floor.yawn: header
    arena.yawn: spec-version
    objective-holon.yawn: spec-version
    routing-proposal.yawn: spec-version
    structural-change-receipt.yawn: spec-version
    turn.yawn: spec-version
    q-space-answer-event.yawn: coordinate
    q-space-frontier-candidate.yawn: coordinate
    q-space-pattern-candidate.yawn: coordinate
    q-space-proof-event.yawn: coordinate
    q-space-question-node.yawn: coordinate
    q-space-transition-event.yawn: coordinate
    collaboration-message.yawn: fragment
    conversation-import-draft.yawn: fragment
    observation.yawn: fragment
    art-brief.v1.yawn: json-contract
    question-proposal.v1.yawn: json-contract

receives:
  - repeated movement patterns
  - proof and boundary constraints
  - agent handoff needs
  - question packet mappings

produces:
  - copyable forms
  - consistent records
  - intake-driven draft frames
  - lower cognitive load
  - versioned state, desire, optional-target, transition, proof, and update shapes

canonical_rule: >
  New templates use attributed state snapshots, first-class desires, optional
  scoped targets, and separate transition intent/result. Legacy current,
  possible, possible_kind, and measurement fields are compatibility aliases.
  Draft 0.2 templates keep arena, one primary parent, typed lateral relations,
  asynchronous turns, routing proposals, and authorized structural receipts
  distinct. Objective Holon 0.1 also keeps candidate, ratification, Yawn, bot,
  and activation distinct. No current human template is marketed as the
  complete .yawn schema. orientation_inquiry presentation fields reference an
  independent orientation_map View and never become semantic state themselves.

questions:
  - what shape should this yawn use
  - which question packet can fill this template
  - what fields are required
  - what can be deleted

links:
